    {
      "id": "br5gRPLJ3_1aAizxIIo8o",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 410.6401127876835,
      "y": 2650.2527714750245,
      "width": 803.9996337890625,
      "height": 13375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bFF",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1959762481,
      "version": 10,
      "versionNonce": 554003071,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790614151117,
      "created": 1790614145682,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "GPT :\n\npublic int maximumSum(int[] a) {  \n    int n = a.length;  \n    int noDel = a[0];  \n    int oneDel = Integer.MIN_VALUE;  \n    int res = a[0];  \n  \n    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {  \n        int prevNoDel = noDel;  \n  \n        noDel = Math.max(a[i], noDel + a[i]);  \n  \n        oneDel = Math.max(prevNoDel, oneDel + a[i]);  \n  \n        res = Math.max(res, Math.max(noDel, oneDel));  \n    }  \n  \n    return res;  \n}  \n\n\n============================================================\nDRY RUN\n============================================================\n\nEx : [1,-2,0,3]\n\n\n// START OF CODE\n\nnoDel = a[0]\n      = 1\n\noneDel = Integer.MIN_VALUE\n       = -∞\n\nres = a[0]\n    = 1\n\n\nInitial:\n\nnoDel  = 1\noneDel = -∞\nres    = 1\n\n\n____________________________________________________________\n\n\nFOR LOOP { // a[1] = -2\n\nprevNoDel = noDel\n          = 1\n\n\na[1] = -2\n\n\nnoDel = max{ a[i], noDel + a[i] }\n\n      = max{ -2, 1 + (-2) }\n\n      = max{ -2, -1 }\n\n      = -1\n\n\n// noDel = -1\n\n\noneDel = max{ prevNoDel, oneDel + a[i] }\n\n       = max{ 1, -∞ + (-2) }\n\n       = max{ 1, -∞ }\n\n       = 1\n\n\n// oneDel = 1\n\n\nres = max{ res, max{noDel, oneDel} }\n\n    = max{ 1, max{-1, 1} }\n\n    = 1\n\n\n// res = 1\n\n\nState after a[1]:\n\nnoDel  = -1\noneDel = 1\nres    = 1\n\n\n____________________________________________________________\n\n\nFOR LOOP { // a[2] = 0\n\nprevNoDel = noDel\n          = -1\n\n\na[2] = 0\n\n\nnoDel = max{ a[i], noDel + a[i] }\n\n      = max{ 0, -1 + 0 }\n\n      = max{ 0, -1 }\n\n      = 0\n\n\n// noDel = 0\n\n\noneDel = max{ prevNoDel, oneDel + a[i] }\n\n       = max{ -1, 1 + 0 }\n\n       = max{ -1, 1 }\n\n       = 1\n\n\n// oneDel = 1\n\n\nres = max{ res, max{noDel, oneDel} }\n\n    = max{ 1, max{0, 1} }\n\n    = 1\n\n\n// res = 1\n\n\nState after a[2]:\n\nnoDel  = 0\noneDel = 1\nres    = 1\n\n\n____________________________________________________________\n\n\nFOR LOOP { // a[3] = 3\n\nprevNoDel = noDel\n          = 0\n\n\na[3] = 3\n\n\nnoDel = max{ a[i], noDel + a[i] }\n\n      = max{ 3, 0 + 3 }\n\n      = max{ 3, 3 }\n\n      = 3\n\n\n// noDel = 3\n\n\noneDel = max{ prevNoDel, oneDel + a[i] }\n\n       = max{ 0, 1 + 3 }\n\n       = max{ 0, 4 }\n\n       = 4\n\n\n// oneDel = 4\n\n\nres = max{ res, max{noDel, oneDel} }\n\n    = max{ 1, max{3, 4} }\n\n    = 4\n\n\n// res = 4\n\n\nState after a[3]:\n\nnoDel  = 3\noneDel = 4\nres    = 4\n\n\n============================================================\nFINAL ANSWER\n============================================================\n\nreturn res;\n\nreturn 4;\n\n\nTherefore:\n\nMaximum Sum = 4\n\n\n============================================================\nVISUALIZATION\n============================================================\n\nArray:\n\n        [ 1    -2    0    3 ]\n               ↓\n             DELETE\n               ↓\n        [ 1     X    0    3 ]\n\nRemaining:\n\n        [ 1     0    3 ]\n\nSum:\n\n        1 + 0 + 3 = 4\n\n\nTherefore:\n\n        Answer = 4\n\n\n============================================================\nVARIABLE VISUALIZATION\n============================================================\n\nThere are TWO tracks:\n\n\n1. noDel\n------------\n\nMeaning:\n\n\"No element has been deleted.\"\n\n\n        1       -2       0       3\n        ↓        ↓       ↓       ↓\n       1       -1       0       3\n\nFinal:\n\nnoDel = 3\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n2. oneDel\n------------\n\nMeaning:\n\n\"Exactly one element has been deleted.\"\n\n\n       -∞       1       1       4\n                ↓       ↓       ↓\n              delete   continue\n               -2\n\n\nFinal:\n\noneDel = 4\n\n\n============================================================\nCOMPLETE VISUAL FLOW\n============================================================\n\n             1       -2       0       3\n             │        │       │       │\n             ↓        ↓       ↓       ↓\n\nnoDel        1       -1       0       3\n\noneDel      -∞        1       1       4\n                       │       │       │\n                       │       │       │\n                       └───────┴───────┘\n                            delete -2\n\n\nFinal:\n\nnoDel  = 3\noneDel = 4\nres    = 4\n\n\n============================================================\nHOW oneDel = 4 HAPPENS\n============================================================\n\nOriginal:\n\n[1, -2, 0, 3]\n\nAt a[1] = -2:\n\noneDel = 1\n\nThis means:\n\n[1, -2]\n    X\n\nDelete -2:\n\n[1]\n\nSum = 1\n\n\nThen a[2] = 0:\n\noneDel = 1 + 0\n       = 1\n\n\nThen a[3] = 3:\n\noneDel = 1 + 3\n       = 4\n\n\nSo:\n\n[1, -2, 0, 3]\n    X\n\n     ↓\n\n[1, 0, 3]\n\n     ↓\n\n1 + 0 + 3\n\n     ↓\n\n     4\n\n\n============================================================\nIMPORTANT: WHY prevNoDel?\n============================================================\n\nWe first store:\n\nprevNoDel = noDel;\n\n\nBecause after this:\n\nnoDel = Math.max(a[i], noDel + a[i]);\n\n\nthe value of noDel changes.\n\n\nFor oneDel:\n\noneDel = Math.max(prevNoDel, oneDel + a[i]);\n\n\nWe need the OLD noDel value.\n\n\nWhy?\n\nBecause:\n\nprevNoDel\n    ↓\nDelete the CURRENT element\n\n\nWhile:\n\noneDel + a[i]\n    ↓\nAlready deleted one element earlier\nand continue with current element.\n\n\n============================================================\nFORMULAS TO REMEMBER\n============================================================\n\nNO DELETE:\n\nnoDel = max(a[i], noDel + a[i])\n\n\nMeaning:\n\nStart a new subarray\n\nOR\n\nContinue the previous subarray.\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nONE DELETE:\n\noneDel = max(prevNoDel, oneDel + a[i])\n\n\nMeaning:\n\nChoice 1:\nDelete the current element.\n\nChoice 2:\nAlready deleted one element earlier,\nso continue with current element.\n\n\n============================================================\nFINAL TABLE\n============================================================\n\nArray = [1,-2,0,3]\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\ni       a[i]    prevNoDel    noDel    oneDel    res\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nStart    1          -           1       -∞       1\n\n  1     -2          1          -1        1       1\n\n  2      0         -1           0        1       1\n\n  3      3          0           3        4       4\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nFINAL:\n\nnoDel  = 3\noneDel = 4\nres    = 4\n\n\n============================================================\nEASY WAY TO REMEMBER\n============================================================\n\nnoDel\n  ↓\nNO deletion\n\n\noneDel\n  ↓\nONE deletion\n\n\nAt every element:\n\n\nnoDel:\n\n        START\n          OR\n       CONTINUE\n\n\noneDel:\n\n       DELETE CURRENT\n            OR\n       CONTINUE AFTER\n       PREVIOUS DELETE\n\n\nFinally:\n\nres = maximum(noDel, oneDel)\n\n\nFor:\n\n[1,-2,0,3]\n\nDelete:\n\n-2\n\n\nRemaining:\n\n[1,0,3]\n\n\nSum:\n\n4\n\n\nFINAL ANSWER = 4",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "GPT :\n\npublic int maximumSum(int[] a) {  \n    int n = a.length;  \n    int noDel = a[0];  \n    int oneDel = Integer.MIN_VALUE;  \n    int res = a[0];  \n  \n    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {  \n        int prevNoDel = noDel;  \n  \n        noDel = Math.max(a[i], noDel + a[i]);  \n  \n        oneDel = Math.max(prevNoDel, oneDel + a[i]);  \n  \n        res = Math.max(res, Math.max(noDel, oneDel));  \n    }  \n  \n    return res;  \n}  \n\n\n============================================================\nDRY RUN\n============================================================\n\nEx : [1,-2,0,3]\n\n\n// START OF CODE\n\nnoDel = a[0]\n      = 1\n\noneDel = Integer.MIN_VALUE\n       = -∞\n\nres = a[0]\n    = 1\n\n\nInitial:\n\nnoDel  = 1\noneDel = -∞\nres    = 1\n\n\n____________________________________________________________\n\n\nFOR LOOP { // a[1] = -2\n\nprevNoDel = noDel\n          = 1\n\n\na[1] = -2\n\n\nnoDel = max{ a[i], noDel + a[i] }\n\n      = max{ -2, 1 + (-2) }\n\n      = max{ -2, -1 }\n\n      = -1\n\n\n// noDel = -1\n\n\noneDel = max{ prevNoDel, oneDel + a[i] }\n\n       = max{ 1, -∞ + (-2) }\n\n       = max{ 1, -∞ }\n\n       = 1\n\n\n// oneDel = 1\n\n\nres = max{ res, max{noDel, oneDel} }\n\n    = max{ 1, max{-1, 1} }\n\n    = 1\n\n\n// res = 1\n\n\nState after a[1]:\n\nnoDel  = -1\noneDel = 1\nres    = 1\n\n\n____________________________________________________________\n\n\nFOR LOOP { // a[2] = 0\n\nprevNoDel = noDel\n          = -1\n\n\na[2] = 0\n\n\nnoDel = max{ a[i], noDel + a[i] }\n\n      = max{ 0, -1 + 0 }\n\n      = max{ 0, -1 }\n\n      = 0\n\n\n// noDel = 0\n\n\noneDel = max{ prevNoDel, oneDel + a[i] }\n\n       = max{ -1, 1 + 0 }\n\n       = max{ -1, 1 }\n\n       = 1\n\n\n// oneDel = 1\n\n\nres = max{ res, max{noDel, oneDel} }\n\n    = max{ 1, max{0, 1} }\n\n    = 1\n\n\n// res = 1\n\n\nState after a[2]:\n\nnoDel  = 0\noneDel = 1\nres    = 1\n\n\n____________________________________________________________\n\n\nFOR LOOP { // a[3] = 3\n\nprevNoDel = noDel\n          = 0\n\n\na[3] = 3\n\n\nnoDel = max{ a[i], noDel + a[i] }\n\n      = max{ 3, 0 + 3 }\n\n      = max{ 3, 3 }\n\n      = 3\n\n\n// noDel = 3\n\n\noneDel = max{ prevNoDel, oneDel + a[i] }\n\n       = max{ 0, 1 + 3 }\n\n       = max{ 0, 4 }\n\n       = 4\n\n\n// oneDel = 4\n\n\nres = max{ res, max{noDel, oneDel} }\n\n    = max{ 1, max{3, 4} }\n\n    = 4\n\n\n// res = 4\n\n\nState after a[3]:\n\nnoDel  = 3\noneDel = 4\nres    = 4\n\n\n============================================================\nFINAL ANSWER\n============================================================\n\nreturn res;\n\nreturn 4;\n\n\nTherefore:\n\nMaximum Sum = 4\n\n\n============================================================\nVISUALIZATION\n============================================================\n\nArray:\n\n        [ 1    -2    0    3 ]\n               ↓\n             DELETE\n               ↓\n        [ 1     X    0    3 ]\n\nRemaining:\n\n        [ 1     0    3 ]\n\nSum:\n\n        1 + 0 + 3 = 4\n\n\nTherefore:\n\n        Answer = 4\n\n\n============================================================\nVARIABLE VISUALIZATION\n============================================================\n\nThere are TWO tracks:\n\n\n1. noDel\n------------\n\nMeaning:\n\n\"No element has been deleted.\"\n\n\n        1       -2       0       3\n        ↓        ↓       ↓       ↓\n       1       -1       0       3\n\nFinal:\n\nnoDel = 3\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n2. oneDel\n------------\n\nMeaning:\n\n\"Exactly one element has been deleted.\"\n\n\n       -∞       1       1       4\n                ↓       ↓       ↓\n              delete   continue\n               -2\n\n\nFinal:\n\noneDel = 4\n\n\n============================================================\nCOMPLETE VISUAL FLOW\n============================================================\n\n             1       -2       0       3\n             │        │       │       │\n             ↓        ↓       ↓       ↓\n\nnoDel        1       -1       0       3\n\noneDel      -∞        1       1       4\n                       │       │       │\n                       │       │       │\n                       └───────┴───────┘\n                            delete -2\n\n\nFinal:\n\nnoDel  = 3\noneDel = 4\nres    = 4\n\n\n============================================================\nHOW oneDel = 4 HAPPENS\n============================================================\n\nOriginal:\n\n[1, -2, 0, 3]\n\nAt a[1] = -2:\n\noneDel = 1\n\nThis means:\n\n[1, -2]\n    X\n\nDelete -2:\n\n[1]\n\nSum = 1\n\n\nThen a[2] = 0:\n\noneDel = 1 + 0\n       = 1\n\n\nThen a[3] = 3:\n\noneDel = 1 + 3\n       = 4\n\n\nSo:\n\n[1, -2, 0, 3]\n    X\n\n     ↓\n\n[1, 0, 3]\n\n     ↓\n\n1 + 0 + 3\n\n     ↓\n\n     4\n\n\n============================================================\nIMPORTANT: WHY prevNoDel?\n============================================================\n\nWe first store:\n\nprevNoDel = noDel;\n\n\nBecause after this:\n\nnoDel = Math.max(a[i], noDel + a[i]);\n\n\nthe value of noDel changes.\n\n\nFor oneDel:\n\noneDel = Math.max(prevNoDel, oneDel + a[i]);\n\n\nWe need the OLD noDel value.\n\n\nWhy?\n\nBecause:\n\nprevNoDel\n    ↓\nDelete the CURRENT element\n\n\nWhile:\n\noneDel + a[i]\n    ↓\nAlready deleted one element earlier\nand continue with current element.\n\n\n============================================================\nFORMULAS TO REMEMBER\n============================================================\n\nNO DELETE:\n\nnoDel = max(a[i], noDel + a[i])\n\n\nMeaning:\n\nStart a new subarray\n\nOR\n\nContinue the previous subarray.\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nONE DELETE:\n\noneDel = max(prevNoDel, oneDel + a[i])\n\n\nMeaning:\n\nChoice 1:\nDelete the current element.\n\nChoice 2:\nAlready deleted one element earlier,\nso continue with current element.\n\n\n============================================================\nFINAL TABLE\n============================================================\n\nArray = [1,-2,0,3]\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\ni       a[i]    prevNoDel    noDel    oneDel    res\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nStart    1          -           1       -∞       1\n\n  1     -2          1          -1        1       1\n\n  2      0         -1           0        1       1\n\n  3      3          0           3        4       4\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nFINAL:\n\nnoDel  = 3\noneDel = 4\nres    = 4\n\n\n============================================================\nEASY WAY TO REMEMBER\n============================================================\n\nnoDel\n  ↓\nNO deletion\n\n\noneDel\n  ↓\nONE deletion\n\n\nAt every element:\n\n\nnoDel:\n\n        START\n          OR\n       CONTINUE\n\n\noneDel:\n\n       DELETE CURRENT\n            OR\n       CONTINUE AFTER\n       PREVIOUS DELETE\n\n\nFinally:\n\nres = maximum(noDel, oneDel)\n\n\nFor:\n\n[1,-2,0,3]\n\nDelete:\n\n-2\n\n\nRemaining:\n\n[1,0,3]\n\n\nSum:\n\n4\n\n\nFINAL ANSWER = 4",
